# The `caos-trace` tool (SPEC, "Tracing"): the std/bash worker image with this
# directory's script curried onto it, plus the `help` an agent registers it by.
# Like `caos-test-result` it reads by hash and touches no source tree.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so editing them re-keys this tool and nothing it
# builds (see std/caos-test/.caos-expr).
HELP=<<END
Print the trace of a run from the hash of its ArgTree: the complete tree of what
happened (`GET /status/<hash>?all=1`) with each node's name, requested / started /
ended times in ms relative to the root, and whether it was REUSED from an earlier
run, followed by a table of the slowest nodes. With `perf`, also print the perf
data workers left at /cas/out-trace. The `caos-test` report prints the hash
beside "full trace" (the one in its `curl .../status/<hash>?all=1` line); a
trace outlives its run and both stacks write to the one redis, so the dev
stack's records are readable from the host's tools.
@param hash The ArgTree hash from the `caos-test` report's "full trace" line (40 hex characters).
@param [perf] Any value: also print every out-trace object found in the tree.
@param [top] How many of the slowest nodes to list (default 25).
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --help=$HELP
